/-!
# The idèle–ideal dictionary of a cycle

`Work.SSGRoute.ZDataMup.Cycle` is the ideal-modulus analogue of the natural-number moduli `m : ℕ`.
This module sets up, for a cycle `c` of `K`, the three subgroups of the group `Frac K` of fractional
ideals of `K` which the idèle–ideal dictionary of Lang's cyclic norm index theorem is phrased in
(the cycle-analogues of `NK.CFTLib.ARL.Icoprime`, `NK.CFTLib.ARL.principalRay` and
`NK.CFTLib.ARL.normIdeals`):

* `Cycle.Icoprime c` — the group `I(c)` of fractional ideals coprime to `c`, as the subgroup of
  `Frac K` whose elements satisfy `Cycle.FracCoprime c`;
* `Cycle.rayOf c` — the congruence ray `P(c)`, image of the principal idèles lying in the
  congruence subgroup `Cycle.congrSubgroup c`;
* `Cycle.normGroupOf K L c cL` — the norm group `𝔑(c)`, generated by the relative norms of the
  integral ideals of `L` coprime to the cycle `cL` over `L`.

The identification of these with the *closure-presented* groups of `CycleDefs.lean`
(`Cycle.idealCoprimeGroup`, `Cycle.principalRay`, `Cycle.normRay`) is carried out in the companion
modules; only `Cycle.principalRay_eq_rayOf` is proved here, since it is immediate from
`Cycle.principalIdele_mem_congrSubgroup_iff`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option linter.style.setOption false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

open scoped NumberField nonZeroDivisors NumberField.LiesOver
open NumberField IsDedekindDomain
